Hey Joaquin,

For the Spectronaut converter, input and annotation parameters refers to the phosphopeptide's experiment's data and experimental design <https://github.com/Vitek-Lab/MSstatsPTM/blob/devel/man/SpectronauttoMSstatsPTMFormat.Rd#L31-L40>.  Then input_protein and annotation_protein refers to the global profiling experiment's data and experimental design <https://github.com/Vitek-Lab/MSstatsPTM/blob/devel/man/SpectronauttoMSstatsPTMFormat.Rd#L45-L49>.

I agree the vignettes need to be updated.  I'm noticing most of the converters in the vignette I linked earlier don't have a sample global profiling proteomic dataset for adjustment (only Fragpipe has it), which makes it difficult to figure out how to incorporate the global profiling adjustment.  We'll update the vignettes to include a sample global profiling dataset for the other converters for the next release.

Tony

